// tap-echo: --close-after 10 --listeners 2
// follows Linux v6.12 tcp_timewait_state_process (TCP_TW_SYN)
// SYN SEQ 5000 is after RCV.NXT 12, allowing reopening without timestamps.
// The old socket closes and the second listener answers SYN-ACK immediately.
// EchoServer relistens Closed sockets; TIME-WAIT still occupies the first socket
// when this SYN arrives. Two sockets keep a listener available.
// The listener derives a fresh ISN (script 0); Linux derives one from the old SND.NXT.
// Entering TIME-WAIT: see scripts/time-wait.pkt.

0     < S 0:0(0) win 64240 <mss 1460,nop,nop,sackOK,nop,wscale 7>
+0    > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,wscale 2,sackOK,eol,eol,eol>
+0    < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 502
+0    < P. 1:11(10) ack 1 win 502
+0    > F. 1:11(10) ack 11 win 32768
+0    < F. 11:11(0) ack 12 win 502
+0    > . 12:12(0) ack 12 win 32768

+1    < S 5000:5000(0) win 64240 <mss 1460,nop,nop,sackOK,nop,wscale 7>
+0    > S. 0:0(0) ack 5001 win 65535 <mss 1460,wscale 2,sackOK,eol,eol,eol>
